<title>FRANCE: ATHLETICS-JURY UPHOLDS DEVERS' DECISION.</title>
<headline>ATHLETICS-JURY UPHOLDS DEVERS' DECISION.</headline>
<text>
<p>PARIS, March 7 ( Reuter) - A jury of appeal upheld a decision to place Olympic women's 100 metres champion Gail Devers in the world indoor 60 metres final on Friday ahead of Greek Ekaterini Thanou.</p>
<p>Both clocked 7.15 in the semifinal and the Greek federation protested to the International Amateur Athletic Federation (IAAF).</p>
<p>&quot;I watched it (the replay) and it was not very clear,&quot; said IAAF secretary general Istvan Gyulai.</p>
<p>The final was scheduled for Friday evening on the first day of the three-day competition.</p>
